  "problems": "Source is the Tommy Hilfiger UK women's size guide, \"TOMMY JEANS SIZES\" section (nz.tommy.com/size_guide_tommy_jeans_womens publishes the same jeans waist/hip ranges plus 36-42). No body/garment wording anywhere, so basis is inferred. Inches tables also exist. Alias conversions overlap (e.g. 25 and 26 are both EU 34 - 36); the US alias in the pants table is published as \"US + UK SIZE 2 - 4\" and a separate \"US SIZE 00 - 0\" row, and the US row was used. INCONSISTENCY: further down the same Tommy Jeans section, tables titled \"JEANS - INSEAM 28/30/32/34\" give a DIFFERENT single-value grading for the same denim sizes (e.g. 27 = waist 67.3, hips 95.3, US 6, EU 36, inside leg 71.1/76.2/81.3/86.4 cm), and a \"SHORTS, SKIRTS, PANTS\" table gives XXS-XL waist 60-80 / hips 86-106. These look like a second (possibly older or US) chart; the jeans version is recorded as the ALTERNATE chart, the shorts/skirts/pants one is not. Confirm which one Tommy Jeans products use before relying on it."
}